==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[appurtenaunce]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|apurtenance|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|apartenance|lang=fro}}, from {{term|apertenir|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|appertineo|appertineō|I belong, I [[appertain]]|lang=la}}.

Cognate to {{term|appertain|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-ncalif-appurtenance.ogg|Audio (Northern California, US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[appendage]] added to something else.
# {{context|in the plural}} [[equipment|Equipment]] used for some specific [[task]]; [[gear]].
# The thing to which another [[pertain|pertains]].
# {{context|legal}} Minor [[property]] (such as an [[outhouse]]) that passes with the main property when it is [[sold]].
# {{context|grammar}} A [[modifier]] that is [[append]]ed or [[prepend]]ed to another word to [[coin]] a new word that expresses belonging.

